  "id": "the-sump-3",
  "_note": "Floor three of the Wextreen Sump. **The digit is not on the map and is not in a place id** — which surveyor's heap a cairn is, is the puzzle, so the ids are positional and the height is in the prose. Nine cairns in the worst order is forty-five card reads; the slab in the middle knows the order and so does the ninth clipboard, which is on the shore two hundred paces from here. **No `outside`**: a floor of the Sump is not one sitting, because its budget is what you brought rather than how tired you are. A save taken here reopens here, and a player who needs a three-by-two from the van can go and get it; what that costs is the walk. **And nothing here names an instrument** — `reach.rs::nothing_in_a_map_file_knows_about_a_survey` refuses one, and it is right to: a map that knew which lens reads it is a map that would have to be edited to add a second.",
